#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:1
msgid "Choosing a level, and raising it later"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:3
msgid ""
"A datum can be written at three levels — a row of a spreadsheet, a block "
"of YAML, or Python — and they **sum** rather than exclude one another, by"
" pipeline name. The question is never \"which level is this format\", it "
"is \"which level is *this reading*\", and a format mixing all three is "
"ordinary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:7
msgid "The rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:9
msgid ""
"**Start at the most constrained level that holds, and go down only where "
"you must. When you go down, write why.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:12
msgid ""
"That last clause is the part that pays. A module whose first line says "
"*what* configuration could not express is a module somebody can delete "
"when the engine grows the cell; a module that says nothing is a module "
"nobody dares touch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:16
msgid "What the levels can say"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "The algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "Its parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "Reach for it when"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "`structured`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "fixed, in the engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "columns of a CSV"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "the reading is the common shape of its datum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "`semistructured`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "named, in the engine or yours"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "YAML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "the reading needs a criterion a cell cannot hold, or an anchor overridden"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "`unstructured`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "yours"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "the reading is a **computation**, not a description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:24
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The practical frontier between the first two is narrower than it sounds. "
"A CSV cell cannot hold a mapping, so a selection written there uses the "
"{doc}`compact grammar <../selections>`; the mapping form in YAML says "
"three things the compact form cannot — the two set operations and "
"`font_of` — and refuses a key it does not know, where a mistyped compact "
"cell can only be caught by the shape of the whole string. A format that "
"needs none of those is better off as a row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:30
msgid "Why the constrained level is worth the effort"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:32
msgid ""
"Because one algorithm with a few parameters covers far more documents "
"than anybody expects, and the project has the count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:35
msgid ""
"`PdfExtractInvestmentsStandard` did not start general. It accumulated "
"logic and parameters to serve documents that kept differing, and today "
"the holdings — the best-covered datum of all — come out like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "measure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "parameters of the algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "4, with a default that leaves only the first required"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "columns of parameters per format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "9, in one CSV"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid "**formats covered**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md
msgid ""
"**26** from the `structured` level, plus fifteen files at the other two "
"calling the same pipe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:45
msgid ""
"Twenty-six formats from one algorithm, at the price of four parameters. "
"Had each variation produced an algorithm of its own, there would be "
"twenty-six to maintain and no pattern for the next one to follow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:49
msgid "How to tell a parameter from an algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:51
msgid "Three questions, in this order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:53
msgid ""
"**Is the logic the same?** If the two cases do the same thing and differ "
"in *where* they look or *how* the value is written, the difference is a "
"**parameter**. If they do different things — reading a ticked box and "
"reading a section heading — they are two algorithms, however many "
"parameters you add."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:57
msgid ""
"**What does the new case cost, and how many does it bring?** One more "
"parameter covering five formats is a bargain; one more branch covering "
"one usually is not. The cost is measured on the **caller** as well: a "
"parameter with a sensible default is not paid for where it is not needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:60
msgid ""
"**Does the parameter describe the variation, or the format?** A parameter"
" called `table` or `company_index` describes the document and "
"generalises. An `if format == \"ARCA-IT24\"` describes **who is "
"calling**, not what is on the page, and never generalises: it is the sign"
" that the grouping is wrong or that the right parameter is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:65
msgid ""
"The limit past which you do not go: **when the algorithm can no longer be"
" explained in a paragraph**, or when its parameters interact in ways that"
" have to be tested in pairs, the complication has outgrown the gain. "
"Split it there — and split it **by logic**, never by format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:69
msgid "Raising the level afterwards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:71
msgid ""
"A reading written in Python because it had to be is not finished "
"business. The project ran one sweep over every author pipeline it had, "
"and the result is the best guide to what tends to move:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:74
msgid ""
"**fifty-one** author pipelines were measured one at a time; **twenty-"
"three** became configuration;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:76
msgid ""
"the largest group was hidden behind a **name**: three formats were "
"calling what looked like three algorithms and were writing the same "
"twelve rows. Renaming it made the group visible, and five portfolio "
"tables became configuration at once;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:79
msgid ""
"the pieces that resisted were not the complicated ones. They were the "
"ones that **compute** — a table whose geometry is recalculated per page —"
" and the ones specific to two formats rather than to a kind of datum;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:82
msgid ""
"what was expected to be delicate, a promise deposited in one segment and "
"resolved in another, was not. What was actually hard is that **the pipes "
"of a segment are concatenated, not composed**: a chain written inside one"
" author function becomes **one** configured pipe with knobs, never three "
"rows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:87
msgid "Proving a promotion changed nothing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:89
msgid ""
"A promotion is a rewrite of a reading that is supposed to read the same, "
"so the burden is invariance, and the suite is not enough on its own:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:92
msgid ""
"**a page fixture compares as a set.** Adding the configured pipe and "
"forgetting to delete the author's one leaves duplicated, identical blocks"
" that collapse, and the per-page tests pass with the pipe running twice. "
"The whole-document test is what sees it;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:95
msgid ""
"**a mechanical rewrite of selections is proven on every page, not on the "
"frozen ones.** Build both forms in a script and compare them line by line"
" — text *and* box — over every page of every test report of the formats "
"involved, before running the suite;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/choosing-a-level.md:98
msgid ""
"**expect the `.log.csv` to move, and predict by how much.** A log line "
"names the pipe that spoke, so promoting a pipe that warns moves that cell"
" at identical message. Count the rows beforehand: on one sweep the count "
"said seven and seven is what moved."
msgstr ""

